# Retail data (user reports 01.11. and 03.11.2026: "different rifle stance for Leon; different camera perspective when
# kicking"; whole-program-status.md, report 6 after 0.96.8: the tables were seen then, not taken over). The shoulder
# camera's default tables g_readyOfs / g_transOfs of the retail main.dol files (read 03.11.2026; US 0x801ff530,
# European 0x80203dd0, the Japanese and Korean ones as the European) differ from the prototype's: Leon's default ready
# table (handguns, rifles) in the middle site (both) and the upper and lower ones (European), Ada's three in two sites
# (both), with the European discs also Leon's other weapons, Leon with Ashley and Krauser's / Wesker's lower sites,
# and Ada's transition in one site (both). CameraQuasiFPS::offsetCorrection sets them before it corrects the tables.
# The debug build's discs keep the prototype's.
